\title{Optimizer}
\meta{toc}{false}

\p{All functional transitions return new state. Keep the returned state for the next call. baux maximizes objective values; negate a loss when minimizing. Coordinate batches use \code{(N, D)} arrays. Standard single-objective search uses \code{(N,)} rewards; multi-output search requires a compatible configuration. \code{complete} currently accepts scalar rewards only.}

\<section>[id]{baux.init}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.init}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.functional}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.init}](docs.html#baux.init)}}
  \pre{
baux.init(
    domain: np.ndarray | PyTreeSpec | Any,
    config: OptimizerConfig | Transform | None = None,
    *,
    pipe: OptimizerConfig | Transform | None = None,
    key: Any = None,
    seed: int | Generator | None = None,
    low: Any = -1.0,
    high: Any = 1.0,
) -> OptimizerState
  }
  \p{Create an optimizer and its initial state.}
  \<dl>[class]{api-contract}{
    \<dt>{Parameters}
    \<dd>{\ul{
      \li{\code{domain}: Coordinate bounds of shape \code{(D, 2)}, a \code{Space}, or a parameter template.}
      \li{\code{config / pipe}: Supply at most one. Without either, uses a TuRBO region, no surrogate and random acquisition.}
      \li{\code{key / seed}: Control the random sequence. \code{key} takes precedence over \code{seed}.}
      \li{\code{low / high}: Bounds for continuous leaves when compiling a parameter template.}
    }}
    \<dt>{Returns}
    \<dd>{An \code{OptimizerState} ready for [\code{ask}](docs.html#baux.ask).}
    \<dt>{Notes}
    \<dd>{Malformed bounds or unsupported configurations raise \code{ValueError}. Use \code{pipe=baux.enn()} to enable an ENN surrogate.}
  }
  \<div>[class]{api-example}{\<p>[class]{example-label}{Example}
\pre{
import numpy as np
import baux

domain = np.array([[-2.0, 2.0], [-2.0, 2.0]])
state = baux.init(domain, seed=42)
for _ in range(6):
    state, batch = baux.ask(state, num_arms=2)
    y = -np.sum(batch.points**2, axis=-1)
    state, _ = baux.tell(state, batch, y)

assert state.num_observations == 12
}
  }
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/functional.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/functional.py#L98)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.ask}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.ask}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.functional}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.ask}](docs.html#baux.ask)}}
  \pre{
baux.ask(
    state: OptimizerState,
    num_arms: int | None = None,
    *,
    n: int | None = None,
) -> tuple[OptimizerState, AskBatch]
  }
  \p{Propose points to evaluate.}
  \<dl>[class]{api-contract}{
    \<dt>{Parameters}
    \<dd>{\ul{
      \li{\code{state}: Current state, including all previous proposals and observations.}
      \li{\code{num_arms / n}: Number of points to propose; defaults to one. Supply at most one name. The count must be positive.}
    }}
    \<dt>{Returns}
    \<dd>{\code{(next_state, batch)}. \code{batch.points} is a read-only \code{(N, D)} array; \code{batch.ids} contains one \code{AskId} per row.}
    \<dt>{Notes}
    \<dd>{Keep \code{next_state} for subsequent calls. Regional proposals become pending in that state. This function does not call the objective. Supplying both count arguments or a nonpositive count raises \code{ValueError}.}
  }
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/functional.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/functional.py#L162)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.tell}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.tell}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.functional}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.tell}](docs.html#baux.tell)}}
  \pre{
baux.tell(
    state: OptimizerState,
    x: Any,
    y: Any,
    *,
    y_var: Any = None,
) -> tuple[OptimizerState, np.ndarray]
  }
  \p{Record an evaluated batch and update the search.}
  \<dl>[class]{api-contract}{
    \<dt>{Parameters}
    \<dd>{\ul{
      \li{\code{state}: State returned by the corresponding \code{ask}.}
      \li{\code{x}: An \code{AskBatch}, \code{(N, D)} coordinate array, one \code{(D,)} point, or parameters matching the state's \code{Space}.}
      \li{\code{y}: Objective values with one row per point. Larger is better. Multiple output columns require a compatible configuration.}
      \li{\code{y_var}: Optional nonnegative, finite observation variances with the same shape as \code{y}.}
    }}
    \<dt>{Returns}
    \<dd>{\code{(next_state, fitted_mu)}. Without a surrogate, \code{fitted_mu} contains the submitted values.}
    \<dt>{Notes}
    \<dd>{For regional search, this is the ordered, whole-batch path. An \code{AskBatch} supplies coordinates here; its ticket IDs are not validated. Use [\code{complete}](docs.html#baux.complete) for ticket-based or out-of-order completion.}
  }
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/functional.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/functional.py#L254)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.step}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.step}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.functional}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.step}](docs.html#baux.step)}}
  \pre{
baux.step(
    state: OptimizerState,
    objective: Callable[[Any], Any],
    *,
    num_arms: int = 1,
    use_pytree: bool = False,
) -> tuple[OptimizerState, np.ndarray]
  }
  \p{Propose, evaluate and record one batch.}
  \<dl>[class]{api-contract}{
    \<dt>{Parameters}
    \<dd>{\ul{
      \li{\code{state}: Current optimizer state.}
      \li{\code{objective}: Called once with a coordinate batch of shape \code{(num_arms, D)}. Return one objective row per arm.}
      \li{\code{num_arms}: Number of points to evaluate.}
      \li{\code{use_pytree}: With a structured domain, pass one decoded tree for one arm, or a tree with stacked leaves for multiple arms.}
    }}
    \<dt>{Returns}
    \<dd>{\code{(next_state, y)} after proposing, evaluating and recording the batch.}
  }
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/functional.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/functional.py#L359)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.complete}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.complete}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.functional}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.complete}](docs.html#baux.complete)}}
  \pre{
baux.complete(
    state: OptimizerState,
    ids: AskBatch | tuple[AskId, ...] | list[AskId],
    y: Any,
    *,
    y_var: Any = None,
) -> OptimizerState
  }
  \p{Record results for pending regional tickets.}
  \<dl>[class]{api-contract}{
    \<dt>{Parameters}
    \<dd>{\ul{
      \li{\code{state}: Regional optimizer state containing the pending tickets.}
      \li{\code{ids}: An \code{AskBatch}, tuple or list of \code{AskId} values.}
      \li{\code{y}: Scalar rewards in ticket order, shape \code{(K,)} or \code{(K, 1)}. Multiple output columns are not supported.}
      \li{\code{y_var}: Optional observation variances with the same shape as \code{y}.}
    }}
    \<dt>{Returns}
    \<dd>{The updated \code{OptimizerState}.}
    \<dt>{Notes}
    \<dd>{A subset may finish before the rest of its batch; batches may finish out of order. Wrong token types raise \code{TypeError}. Unknown, duplicated, resolved or invalidated tickets are rejected. A region restart invalidates that region's old tickets.}
  }
  \<div>[class]{api-example}{\<p>[class]{example-label}{Example}
\pre{
import numpy as np
import baux

domain = np.array([[-1.0, 1.0], [-1.0, 1.0]])
pipe = baux.enn(k=5) | baux.regions(2)
state = baux.init(domain, pipe, seed=42)
state, batch = baux.ask(state, num_arms=4)
assert len(state.pending_ids) == 4
state = baux.complete(state, batch.ids[:2], np.array([0.5, 0.8]))
state = baux.cancel(state, batch.ids[2:])
assert len(state.pending_ids or ()) == 0
}
  }
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/functional.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/functional.py#L276)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.cancel}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.cancel}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.functional}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.cancel}](docs.html#baux.cancel)}}
  \pre{
baux.cancel(
    state: OptimizerState,
    ids: AskBatch | tuple[AskId, ...] | list[AskId],
) -> OptimizerState
  }
  \p{Retire pending regional tickets without an observation.}
  \<dl>[class]{api-contract}{
    \<dt>{Parameters}
    \<dd>{\ul{
      \li{\code{state}: Regional optimizer state containing the pending tickets.}
      \li{\code{ids}: An \code{AskBatch}, tuple or list of \code{AskId} values to retire.}
    }}
    \<dt>{Returns}
    \<dd>{The updated \code{OptimizerState}, without adding observations or counting a trust-region failure.}
    \<dt>{Notes}
    \<dd>{Cancellation changes optimizer bookkeeping. The caller must stop any external job.}
  }
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/functional.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/functional.py#L309)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.restart_region}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.restart_region}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.functional}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.restart_region}](docs.html#baux.restart_region)}}
  \pre{
baux.restart_region(
    state: OptimizerState,
    slot: int,
    center: Any,
) -> tuple[OptimizerState, tuple[AskId, ...]]
  }
  \p{Start a regional slot again at a supplied center.}
  \<dl>[class]{api-contract}{
    \<dt>{Parameters}
    \<dd>{\ul{
      \li{\code{state}: A regional optimizer state; other configurations raise \code{RuntimeError}.}
      \li{\code{slot}: Index of the region to restart.}
      \li{\code{center}: One \code{(D,)} coordinate point or a structured parameter value.}
    }}
    \<dt>{Returns}
    \<dd>{\code{(next_state, abandoned_ids)}. Pending evaluations in that region are invalidated.}
    \<dt>{Notes}
    \<dd>{The caller owns external jobs and decides whether to cancel them.}
  }
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/functional.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/functional.py#L326)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.import_observations}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.import_observations}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.functional}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.import_observations}](docs.html#baux.import_observations)}}
  \pre{
baux.import_observations(
    state: OptimizerState,
    x: Any,
    y: Any,
    *,
    y_var: Any = None,
) -> tuple[OptimizerState, np.ndarray]
  }
  \p{Add measurements collected outside the current pending batch.}
  \<dl>[class]{api-contract}{
    \<dt>{Parameters}
    \<dd>{\ul{
      \li{\code{state}: Current optimizer state.}
      \li{\code{x / y / y_var}: Coordinates, measurements and optional variances, using the same shapes as [\code{tell}](docs.html#baux.tell).}
    }}
    \<dt>{Returns}
    \<dd>{\code{(next_state, fitted_mu)} after adding the observations.}
    \<dt>{Notes}
    \<dd>{Does not complete pending tickets. Use for historical data or an explicitly chosen import of a late result.}
  }
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/functional.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/functional.py#L265)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.posterior_mu}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.posterior_mu}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.functional}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.posterior_mu}](docs.html#baux.posterior_mu)}}
  \pre{
baux.posterior_mu(state: OptimizerState, x: Any) -> np.ndarray
  }
  \p{Predict the fitted surrogate mean at query points.}
  \<dl>[class]{api-contract}{
    \<dt>{Parameters}
    \<dd>{\ul{
      \li{\code{state}: Optimizer state with a fitted surrogate.}
      \li{\code{x}: Query coordinates of shape \code{(N, D)}, or parameters matching the state's domain.}
    }}
    \<dt>{Returns}
    \<dd>{A read-only NumPy array of predicted means in the objective's units. Does not advance the optimizer.}
  }
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/functional.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/functional.py#L350)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.OptimizerState}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.OptimizerState}[data-kind]{class}[data-module]{baux.functional}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.OptimizerState}](docs.html#baux.OptimizerState)}}
  \pre{
class baux.OptimizerState  (frozen dataclass; constructed via baux.init)
  }
  \p{The state returned by the functional optimizer.}
  \p{Create it with [\code{init}](docs.html#baux.init). Each transition returns a new state; retain the old one only if you need a branch or checkpoint.}
  \p{\code{x_obs}, \code{y_obs}: observation arrays. \code{num_observations}, \code{num_regions}, \code{tr_length}: current search information. \code{best_x}, \code{best_params}, \code{best_y}: incumbent coordinates, decoded parameters and value, or \code{None} before observations.}
  \p{\code{pending_ids}: raw integer IDs for inspection; pass the typed \code{batch.ids} to \code{complete} or \code{cancel}. \code{fork(key=None, *, seed=None)} creates another search branch. [Checkpoints and keys](api-state.html) covers persistence and branching.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/state.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/state.py#L143)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.AskBatch}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.AskBatch}[data-kind]{class}[data-module]{baux.bo}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.AskBatch}](docs.html#baux.AskBatch)}}
  \pre{
baux.AskBatch(
    ids: tuple[AskId, ...],
    points: np.ndarray,
    spec: Any = None,
    weights: np.ndarray | None = None,
)
  }
  \p{Points and evaluation identities returned by a proposal.}
  \p{\code{points}: read-only \code{(N, D)} coordinates. \code{ids}: one \code{AskId} per row. \code{len(batch)} is \code{N}.}
  \p{\code{params}: tuple of decoded parameter trees, one per row. \code{stacked}: one tree with a leading batch axis on its leaves. For an unstructured domain, these expose the coordinate rows and matrix.}
  \p{Keep the batch paired with the state returned by \code{ask}. Tickets support asynchronous completion only when regional search is enabled.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/bo.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/bo.py#L42)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.AskId}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.AskId}[data-kind]{class}[data-module]{baux.bo}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.AskId}](docs.html#baux.AskId)}}
  \pre{
baux.AskId(value: int)
  }
  \p{An opaque evaluation ticket.}
  \p{Keep tokens returned in \code{batch.ids} and pass them back unchanged. \code{aid.value} exposes the unsigned 64-bit integer for inspection. Tickets are immutable, hashable and ordered.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/bo.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/bo.py#L25)}
}

